/-
The generic test driver (kit v2, `notes/kit-v2.md` decisions 1-3), proved once.

A kit's client node runs `Main`, generated by `harness/kitgen` as one call
`driver.Run(Addrs(), New, Op, Gen, check.X, NC, K, Start, WaitMs)`
(`harness/driver/driver.go`). Here:

* `DriverKit M`: the kit's code as the statement refers to it: its test package (where `New`,
  `Op`, `Gen`, `Start`, `Addrs` and `Main` live), the address constants, the constants `nC`, `k`,
  `waitMs`, the encodings of the model's inputs and outputs, the input premise, and the names of
  the functions `Main` passes to the driver.
* `DriverClientSpec M K start`: what a run proves of the kit's functions (decision 2), stated on
  the function values (`@! K.newF` etc.): the package's initialization, `New` on the address
  slice from the client node's share `start` (one token per client, `client_tok γ c 0`), `Op`
  logically atomic at `↑clientN` in M1's B form (`(encO o, true)`, or `(_, false)` an unknown
  outcome) for client `c`'s `j`-th operation, `j < k` (an operation budget: `Main` makes `k` per
  client, so `Op` takes `client_tok γ c j` to `client_tok γ c (j + 1)` only for `j < k`), `Gen`
  (an encoded input meeting the premise) and `Start` (any number). `DriverClientSpec0` is the
  budget-free form (`client_tok γ c`, kept by `Op`), the form of runs before the budget;
  `DriverClientSpec0.toSpec` gives a `DriverClientSpec` from it.
* `wp_driver_Run`: `driver.Run`'s spec, from a client spec, a checker spec and `clients.Run`'s
  spec (M1's `wp_Run`).
* `mainImpl`: the goose translation of the generated `Main`, as a function of the names it
  mentions; a kit's `Main.impl` is `mainImpl ...` by `rfl`.
* `DriverMainFacts`: the per-kit facts the generic lemma needs, each generated by kitgen and
  proved by a fixed script (`Main.impl`'s form, `Addrs()`'s slice, the package closure's
  `get_is_pkg_init`, the dependencies' `isPkgInit`, the import assumptions, the checker, the
  bounds on `nC` and `k`).
* `driver_boot`: the client node's boot WP from a client spec and the facts.
* `DriverDistSpec`, `driver_dist_safe`: as `DistSpec` and `harness_dist_safe`
  (`Harness/DistLemma.lean`), with the client spec over the kit's functions, given the client
  node's IP (`netIp = ip.spell` for `cfg.ips[0]`, the fact `nodeIp` the servers get too); the
  generic lemma for every kit whose `Main` is the generated one.
-/
module

public import Harness.DistLemma
public import Harness.WriteOnceChecker
public import Harness.GeneratedProof.dsverify_lab.harness.driver
public import Harness.Proof.log
public import Perennial.Proof.time

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

namespace Perennial

open Iris Iris.BI Iris.ProgramLogic Iris.Std ProofMode NetConn Dsv

namespace dsverify_lab.harness

set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false

